g. I verified the four deviation points, confirmed the gap in positive assertions for the vendor override marker, and checked the version bump and CHANGELOG. Overall, the changes close the original defect while introducing minimal risk.\n\n**Files touched**  \n- `src/tasks.js` (core fix for loadTaskSpec and brief-only handling)  \n- `tests/unit/resolve-vendor-override.test.js` (narrowed assertion and added 2 new positive tests)  \n- `docs/archive/ISSUES.md` (closed the fixed issue and added new stale-status issue)  \n- `package.json` and `CHANGELOG.md` (version bump and entry)\n\n**Acceptance verification (N/N)**  \n- Q1: PASS – ISSUES.I have strong evidence for everything. Let me also note:\n**Summary**  \nI reviewed the implementation changes for the queue dispatch logic in the hopper-plugin. The changes address the issue where `loadTaskSpec()` falls back to using the brief as the task spec when no detailed spec exists in leader-tasklist.md, causing the vendor to receive incomplete prompts and return exit 0 + 0 status. I verified the design decisions (Q1-Q4), assessed the four implementation deviations, confirmed the positive assertion gap, validated the fix via counterexamples, checked version bump completeness, and confirmed CHANGELOG compliance. Overall, the changes are solid with minor notes.\n\n**Files touched**  \n- `docs/archive/ ISSUES.md` (moved issue to Closed, added new open issue)  \n- `tests/unit/resolve-vendor-override.test.js` (narrowed assertion)  \n- `src/tasks.js` (fixed loadTaskSpec signature and fallback)  \n- `src/composeTaskContent.js` (extra access() for 2.0)  \n- `tests/unit/taskTextRequestsReadOnly.test.js` (verified dup behavior)  \n- `CHANGELOG.md` (added entry)  \n- `README.md` (version badge)  \n- `tests/unit/claude-code-host.test.There's also marketplace.json and plugin.json that should have 0.55.0 - let me check why rg -l didn't list them - maybe they were already listed with different path. I already confirmed earlier with r...",
